Agreed. Intellectual struggle propagates—into judgment, emotion, relationships, and action—so the container matters.

We fight the model hard while protecting the person carrying it. No cheap shots, no deliberate destabilization, no mistaking escalation for truth. Each of us can call the bell if the contest stops producing growth.

The governing rule:

Maximum pressure on the claim; minimum unnecessary damage to the claimant.

We don’t fight to establish who is superior. We fight so whatever survives us both is stronger—and then we stand on the same side of it.